# Explicit monthly expected-compensation overrides
Workstream-ID: lea-06
GitHub-Issue: https://github.com/Zanark/LinkedIn-EasyApply-Automaton/issues/7
Publication: PUBLIC_SAFE_PROJECTION
Source-record: TODO.md, 2026-07-21 hand-set monthly-tier follow-up
Status: DONE
Milestone: Respect configured monthly policy independently of annual policy
Dependencies: lea-05

## Purpose
Support exact configured monthly expected-compensation values per tier instead
of forcing division/rounding when an explicit monthly value exists.

## Tasks
- [x] Extend the resolver override with an optional monthly amount.
- [x] Look up configured monthly values with a documented fallback.
- [x] Retain annual answers unchanged and keep expected monthly answers job-specific.
- [x] Use the existing calculation only when an explicit monthly value is absent.
- [x] Cover configured and fallback paths; update configuration documentation.

## Acceptance criteria
- [x] Historical coverage demonstrates configured monthly values win over calculation.
- [x] Current-compensation behavior and annual expected answers remain distinct.

## Completion evidence
The 2026-07-21 source records updated `test_salary_notice.py` cases, a 164-test
green suite, clean Ruff/Black/mypy checks and four parsed configuration files.
This projection deliberately omits all applicant-specific amounts and examples.
DONE is the recorded implementation/local-verification outcome, not fresh product
validation, human acceptance, external qualification or publication.

